# Architecture-first changes

Before any edit, read `ARCHITECTURE.md` and the repo layout. Identify the owning module.

Do not shortcut the flow: bots/CLI/API → MatchingEngine → OrderBook → trades. Bots never write the book. Frontend and API contain no matching logic.

Do not change matching rules, engine API (`submit`, `cancel`, `book`, `trades`), Order/Trade fields, `Decimal` prices, or module boundaries without updating `ARCHITECTURE.md` in the same change.

After edits, run `pytest` including invalid inputs (qty ≤ 0, bad price, unknown side, duplicate id, empty symbol, missing cancel) and flow regressions (same-side, FIFO, partials, cancels, empty book). Never commit failing tests or architecture contradictions.
